# T11i: notes on the live channel play the focused role and release.
#
# In STUDIO and LIVE external MIDI notes play the focused role through the held-note table; the
# default focus is BASS. Program Change, the clock and the per-part channels are the other
# scenarios. Nothing here is flashed (host only).
wait 300
expect focus 1                                  # BASS by default
expect midiheld 0
# omni (the default): a note on any channel plays the focused role and releases
midi 90 3C 64
wait 50
expect midiheld 1
midi 80 3C 00
wait 200
expect midiheld 0
# a fixed channel (3): channel 3 reaches the app, channel 1 is ignored
midicfg 3 0
wait 20
midi 90 3C 64
wait 50
expect midiheld 0
midi 92 3C 64
wait 50
expect midiheld 1
midi 82 3C 00
wait 50
expect midiheld 0
# the focused role is CHORDS (FM6) here: it plays and releases to zero voices
midicfg 0 0
wait 20
press PLAY
wait 700
release PLAY
wait 20
turn ALGO 2 80                                  # BASS -> CHORDS
expect focus 3
press PLAY
wait 700
release PLAY
wait 50
expect mode 0
midi 90 3C 64
midi 90 40 64
wait 50
expect fm6held 2
midi 80 3C 00
midi 80 40 00
wait 2000
expect fm6held 0
expect fm6voices 0
expect midiheld 0
dump midi_notes.json
